# Generated source bundles - regenerate with tools-export-source.py
*-source-code.txt
*-source-code.zip
buffer-cards/

# Android signing keys. A keystore in git history is a keystore that is public
# forever, even after a later delete. Never commit one.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/android-upload.keystore
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/*.keystore
# Bubblewrap build output and its downloaded toolchain
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/app/
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/build/
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/.gradle/
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/*.aab
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/*.apk
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/twa/*.idsig

# Generated by reference/competitor-watch.js — a report, not source
reference/watch-report.md

# Python bytecode caches — never useful in the repo
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Page images built by tools-md-to-pdf.py --png. Regenerate them, don't commit
# them — 95 PNGs of documents that are already in the repo as markdown.
*-pages/

# NO VIDEO FILES IN THIS REPO (rule, 27 Aug 2026). All 39 were purged from
# tracking - talking heads, AI pieces, samples, the whole library, 246 MB.
# Jacques keeps them in his own file and on social media; they are handed to
# him in chat instead.
#
# UPDATED 31 Aug 2026 - "we dont push videos no more only music" (Jacques).
# MUSIC AND AUDIO STAY: content/score/, TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/audio/.
# The RENDER TOOLING STAYS: tools/render-film.js, prep-still.py, make-film.py.
# EVERYTHING ELSE ABOUT A VIDEO IS HANDED OVER IN CHAT, NOT COMMITTED - the
# .mp4, the *-source.html, and the stills. This REPLACES the 27 Aug line that
# kept sources and stills here so pieces could be rebuilt from the repo.
# Already-tracked files are NOT affected by the line below; it only stops a
# future session committing a NEW source by accident, the same way the video
# extensions have since 27 Aug.
content/*-source.html
content/a18/
content/a19/
content/binge-night/
content/couple/
content/film-engine/
content/food/
content/library/
content/pills/
content/supporter-husband/
content/worry/
content/endcard-template.html
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv

# The user database and its backups. These hold real people's journals,
# cravings and emails; a database committed once is in the history forever,
# even after a later delete. Running the server locally creates both.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
TurnSomeDayIntoOneday/server/backups/
